WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.370 --> 01:34.930
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.259 --> 01:37.740
[Episode 59]

4
01:38.229 --> 01:39.150
Comrades,

5
01:39.710 --> 01:42.370
we've had people in each company try wild plants

6
01:42.640 --> 01:44.440
to help you learn to tell

7
01:44.460 --> 01:45.360
which wild plants are safe to eat

8
01:45.360 --> 01:47.020
and which ones are poisonous.

9
01:47.590 --> 01:48.650
Plants like these,

10
01:48.710 --> 01:50.759
aconite, wolf's bane,

11
01:51.430 --> 01:53.000
and lousewort

12
01:53.000 --> 01:54.560
are all poisonous. Don't eat them. Remember that.

13
01:54.560 --> 01:55.130
Okay.

14
01:55.920 --> 01:57.590
Stay strong. You mustn't fall asleep.

15
01:57.590 --> 01:58.680
Don't sleep!

16
01:59.920 --> 02:00.710
Hongxia!

17
02:01.280 --> 02:02.880
Hongxia, don't fall asleep!

18
02:03.310 --> 02:04.430
Hongxia, wake up!

19
02:04.790 --> 02:05.790
Hang in there!

20
02:06.150 --> 02:06.710
Hongxia!

21
02:11.400 --> 02:14.120
My dear comrades, you mustn't sleep!

22
02:14.470 --> 02:16.840
Don't fall asleep, everyone!

23
02:19.560 --> 02:20.820
Commander-in-Chief.

24
02:22.079 --> 02:26.280
Give us another little Sichuan opera performance.

25
02:27.910 --> 02:29.170
Commander-in-Chief!

26
02:29.560 --> 02:31.450
Could you perform another piece of Jinqianban,

27
02:31.450 --> 02:33.970
a traditional folk art from our hometown?

28
02:35.230 --> 02:36.070
Sure.

29
02:37.630 --> 02:38.430
I'll sing.

30
02:41.190 --> 02:42.630
But there's one condition.

31
02:42.630 --> 02:44.360
You have to hold on while I sing.

32
02:44.430 --> 02:45.630
No dozing off.

33
02:45.890 --> 02:48.730
You all look absolutely famished.

34
02:48.960 --> 02:51.000
You've become so terribly thin.

35
02:51.310 --> 02:52.670
I'll sing you a song about someone fat.

36
02:52.670 --> 02:54.550
It's called "The Fat Lady."

37
02:59.360 --> 03:01.590
There once was a lady

38
03:02.000 --> 03:04.310
whose surname was Pang.

39
03:04.410 --> 03:09.040
She lived in Pang Village.

40
03:09.350 --> 03:12.000
And just how fat was this lady?

41
03:12.020 --> 03:14.180
Fat as could be,

42
03:14.630 --> 03:16.720
with quite a reputation.

43
03:16.800 --> 03:21.190
Her head was as big as a city gate.

44
03:21.840 --> 03:23.590
And her teeth were as long as...

45
03:30.120 --> 03:30.710
Li.

46
03:30.710 --> 03:31.560
Li!

47
03:31.800 --> 03:32.590
Li!

48
03:34.400 --> 03:35.310
Li.

49
04:01.310 --> 04:06.590
Her teeth were as long as carrying poles.

50
04:07.190 --> 04:11.430
Whenever the lady cleared her throat,

51
04:12.470 --> 04:17.870
nine walls would come crashing down.

52
04:18.120 --> 04:20.600
Some thought they'd heard cannons firing.

53
04:20.600 --> 04:23.800
Others thought the city walls had fallen.

54
04:24.680 --> 04:26.680
Fat Lady, oh, Fat Lady.

55
04:27.310 --> 04:29.480
She had herself a brand-new dress.

56
04:29.870 --> 04:32.270
Thirty-six bolts of indigo cloth

57
04:32.390 --> 04:36.950
still weren't long enough to cover her legs.

58
04:37.430 --> 04:39.430
Ten yards of indigo cloth

59
04:39.750 --> 04:41.190
were cut and sewn

60
04:41.870 --> 04:43.750
into a pair of

61
04:44.159 --> 04:45.920
shoe uppers.

62
04:46.360 --> 04:50.240
With her left foot in Chengdu,

63
04:50.310 --> 04:52.750
one stretch of her right leg

64
04:52.750 --> 04:57.680
and she'd reach Guiyang.

65
06:16.310 --> 06:24.730
♪ Mama calls me home for supper ♪

66
06:25.280 --> 06:34.260
♪ And I want to count the stars above ♪

67
06:35.280 --> 06:44.310
♪ Each one twinkling so bright ♪

68
06:44.790 --> 06:53.860
♪ Flickering as they winked at me ♪

69
06:55.130 --> 06:59.950
♪ One little star ♪

70
06:59.980 --> 07:04.010
♪ Two little stars ♪

71
07:05.420 --> 07:14.100
♪ With starlight to guide me, I fear no road ♪

72
07:14.960 --> 07:23.980
♪ I walked until the rooster crowed at dawn ♪

73
07:24.420 --> 07:35.260
♪ Little stars hide and play peekaboo with me ♪

74
08:48.400 --> 08:49.640
Erzhu.

75
08:49.780 --> 08:50.820
Erzhu.

76
09:35.730 --> 09:37.160
Comrade Niu Erzhu.

77
09:38.290 --> 09:40.250
Your mission is accomplished.

78
09:41.250 --> 09:42.980
Now it's time to change shifts.

79
09:44.810 --> 09:46.340
We'll take over.

80
10:48.030 --> 10:50.320
At the end of July 1936,

81
10:50.510 --> 10:52.240
the 2nd and 4th Front Armies

82
10:52.260 --> 10:54.200
finally made it out of the grasslands

83
10:54.200 --> 10:56.240
after an arduous journey

84
10:56.320 --> 10:57.920
and tremendous sacrifices.

85
10:58.510 --> 10:59.960
Following the Central Committee's orders,

86
10:59.960 --> 11:02.080
they recaptured Baozuo for the second time.

87
11:02.080 --> 11:03.090
In early August,

88
11:03.320 --> 11:04.740
the Northwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee

89
11:04.740 --> 11:07.190
held a meeting at Qiuji Temple in Baozuo.

90
11:07.320 --> 11:09.320
It was decided, in accordance with the Central Committee's instructions,

91
11:09.320 --> 11:11.520
to officially launch the

92
11:11.750 --> 11:14.410
Minzhou, Taozhou and Xigu Campaign on August 5.

93
11:14.600 --> 11:17.320
On August 9, the vanguard of the 4th Front Army,

94
11:17.320 --> 11:19.450
the 88th Division, captured Lazikou.

95
11:19.880 --> 11:20.720
The 89th Division

96
11:20.720 --> 11:23.670
then captured Dacaotan and Hadapu.

97
11:24.120 --> 11:26.770
Shortly afterward, with the 4th Front Army leading the way

98
11:26.770 --> 11:28.270
and the 2nd Front Army following behind,

99
11:28.270 --> 11:30.270
they advanced into southern Gansu.

100
11:30.670 --> 11:31.890
Meanwhile,

101
11:32.360 --> 11:34.200
the Guangdong-Guangxi Incident, led by Chen Jitang, Li Zongren,

102
11:34.200 --> 11:36.120
Bai Chongxi and others

103
11:36.200 --> 11:39.360
in the name of resisting Japan and saving the nation,

104
11:39.870 --> 11:43.240
was rapidly losing momentum under Chiang Kai-shek's

105
11:43.480 --> 11:45.480
military and political pressure.

106
11:45.900 --> 11:49.100
Since Chen Jitang announced his resignation in mid-July

107
11:49.150 --> 11:52.390
and Guangdong came under the control of the Nanjing Nationalist Government,

108
11:52.390 --> 11:55.120
Guangxi, governed by Li Zongren and Bai Chongxi,

109
11:55.170 --> 11:57.170
was left struggling to stand alone.

110
11:57.730 --> 12:01.860
[Whampoa, Guangzhou]

111
11:58.360 --> 11:59.240
General Liu.

112
11:59.440 --> 12:01.080
The Generalissimo has repeatedly stressed

113
12:01.080 --> 12:03.870
that the Nationalist Government is determined to resist Japan.

114
12:03.870 --> 12:06.120
But shouldn't we pacify the interior before resisting foreign aggression?

115
12:06.120 --> 12:07.150
How can we fight Japan

116
12:07.150 --> 12:08.360
without first eliminating the Communists

117
12:08.360 --> 12:09.820
and unifying the country?

118
12:10.640 --> 12:13.530
The Generalissimo says we must pacify the country before resisting Japan.

119
12:13.530 --> 12:15.480
But Mr. Li (Zongren) and Mr. Bai (Chongxi)

120
12:15.480 --> 12:16.750
believe that if we resist Japan first,

121
12:16.750 --> 12:18.330
internal stability will follow naturally.

122
12:18.330 --> 12:19.880
If we keep fighting among ourselves

123
12:19.880 --> 12:21.220
in the name of securing internal stability,

124
12:21.220 --> 12:23.220
the Japanese will be the ones to benefit.

125
12:21.260 --> 12:24.420
[Liu Fei, Guangxi Clique Negotiator]

126
12:23.690 --> 12:25.290
Weizhang (Liu Fei).

127
12:26.000 --> 12:27.670
Internal pacification is meant to prepare us to resist Japan.

128
12:27.670 --> 12:28.360
Just look.

129
12:28.440 --> 12:31.150
If every province refuses to obey the central government

130
12:31.150 --> 12:32.030
and acts on its own,

131
12:32.030 --> 12:33.320
without making thorough preparations,

132
12:33.320 --> 12:34.960
and rushes into war against Japan,

133
12:34.960 --> 12:36.390
wouldn't that be tantamount to suicide?

134
12:36.390 --> 12:37.670
Japan's appetite is insatiable.

135
12:37.670 --> 12:39.000
Its ambitions know no bounds.

136
12:39.000 --> 12:39.840
While we are making preparations,

137
12:39.840 --> 12:41.840
the Japanese army is preparing too.

138
12:41.870 --> 12:43.320
And our resources and capabilities

139
12:43.320 --> 12:45.030
can never keep pace with theirs.

140
12:45.030 --> 12:47.030
If we go on preparing indefinitely,

141
12:47.150 --> 12:49.320
when exactly will we be ready?

142
12:49.460 --> 12:52.190
Surely the Generalissimo must give us an answer.

143
12:52.530 --> 12:54.570
My position has always been clear.

144
12:59.180 --> 13:01.410
First and foremost, you must unconditionally

145
13:01.410 --> 13:03.810
obey the orders of the central government.

146
13:04.420 --> 13:05.850
[Qian Dajun, Director of the First Department, Chairman's Office,]

147
13:04.550 --> 13:05.680
From this moment on,

148
13:05.850 --> 13:07.290
[Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

149
13:06.360 --> 13:07.870
as long as the Japanese make no further advances,

150
13:07.870 --> 13:09.600
we will continue our preparations.

151
13:09.600 --> 13:11.240
We will not provoke a war.

152
13:11.240 --> 13:13.600
But if the Japanese dare to advance even one step,

153
13:13.600 --> 13:14.930
we will fight the moment

154
13:15.390 --> 13:16.510
they do.

155
13:17.630 --> 13:19.870
Generalissimo, I understand what you mean now.

156
13:19.870 --> 13:21.630
As long as the preparations are not open-ended,

157
13:21.630 --> 13:22.550
when I get back,

158
13:22.550 --> 13:23.910
I can persuade Mr. Li and Mr. Bai

159
13:23.910 --> 13:26.380
to bring the conflict to an end as soon as possible.

160
13:26.380 --> 13:28.090
I'd like to ask you a favor.

161
13:28.550 --> 13:29.480
When you return,

162
13:29.630 --> 13:30.270
please pass on a message

163
13:30.270 --> 13:32.110
from me to Delin (Li Zongren) and Jiansheng (Bai Chongxi).

164
13:32.110 --> 13:32.960
Tell them

165
13:32.980 --> 13:35.240
that as long as they agree to a ceasefire,

166
13:35.310 --> 13:37.200
they can name whatever terms they want.

167
13:37.200 --> 13:37.890
Yes, sir.

168
13:52.910 --> 13:53.720
It looks like

169
13:54.280 --> 13:56.310
Li and Bai

170
13:56.510 --> 13:58.570
won't be able to hold out much longer.

171
13:58.840 --> 13:59.630
Once the two provinces are brought under control,

172
13:59.630 --> 14:00.870
we'll have nothing to worry about in the south.

173
14:00.870 --> 14:03.000
Then we can eliminate the Communist Army without any distractions.

174
14:03.000 --> 14:04.030
We must never

175
14:04.200 --> 14:06.200
underestimate the Communist Army.

176
14:06.320 --> 14:08.630
Based on the intelligence we've gathered,

177
14:08.630 --> 14:10.100
we've identified a problem.

178
14:10.100 --> 14:12.120
The Red Army entrenched in northern Shaanxi

179
14:12.120 --> 14:14.720
may have already resolved its internal divisions.

180
14:14.720 --> 14:17.290
It is now like a giant magnet,

181
14:17.320 --> 14:18.620
drawing in He Long's forces

182
14:18.620 --> 14:20.770
as well as Zhang Guotao's troops.

183
14:21.090 --> 14:23.040
We absolutely cannot allow that to happen.

184
14:23.040 --> 14:24.670
Yes, sir. We won't underestimate them.

185
14:24.670 --> 14:25.380
Muyin (Qian Dajun).

186
14:25.380 --> 14:25.950
Yes, sir!

187
14:25.980 --> 14:28.710
Send telegrams in my name to Hu Zongnan, Wang Jun,

188
14:28.830 --> 14:30.190
and Mao Bingwen.

189
14:30.480 --> 14:32.670
Tell them to seize the

190
14:32.720 --> 14:33.960
Jingning, Huining and Dingxi areas

191
14:33.960 --> 14:34.750
alongside

192
14:34.790 --> 14:36.860
the Xi'an-Lanzhou Highway at all costs,

193
14:36.860 --> 14:38.320
and cut off the Communist Army's route to rendezvous.

194
14:38.320 --> 14:40.080
Yes, sir. I'll see to it at once.

195
14:52.990 --> 14:53.850
Comrade Luofu.

196
14:54.450 --> 14:55.130
Comrade Enlai.

197
14:55.130 --> 14:55.930
Comrade Enlai!

198
14:55.930 --> 14:56.560
Comrade Jiaxiang.

199
14:56.560 --> 14:57.620
You're here early.

200
14:58.150 --> 14:59.720
These are letters from Comrade Zedong.

201
14:59.720 --> 15:03.000
Let everyone take a look and see if anything has been overlooked.

202
15:03.000 --> 15:03.860
Comrade Zedong

203
15:03.960 --> 15:05.670
was up all night again, I see.

204
15:05.750 --> 15:07.030
Yang Hucheng, Fu Zuoyi,

205
15:07.030 --> 15:09.200
Song Ziwen, Han Fuju, Zhang Zizhong.

206
15:09.870 --> 15:12.550
Comrade Zedong has written to all those we need to win over.

207
15:12.550 --> 15:14.550
I don't think anyone has been overlooked.

208
15:14.550 --> 15:15.670
The one we should win over most of all...

209
15:15.670 --> 15:16.390
Come, sit down.

210
15:16.390 --> 15:18.320
is Generalissimo Chiang himself.

211
15:18.360 --> 15:20.220
Unfortunately, he won't listen.

212
15:20.270 --> 15:22.200
He's sending more and more troops to northern Shaanxi,

213
15:22.200 --> 15:23.140
tightening the noose around us.

214
15:23.140 --> 15:25.340
We can't break out of his encirclement,

215
15:25.360 --> 15:26.840
and fighting our way out won't be easy either.

216
15:26.840 --> 15:29.590
That's why our 3 main forces must reunite as soon as possible

217
15:29.590 --> 15:30.550
and join forces.

218
15:30.750 --> 15:33.290
That would allow us to defend the Shaanxi-Gansu base area

219
15:33.290 --> 15:35.790
and withstand Chiang Kai-shek's encirclement campaigns.

220
15:35.790 --> 15:38.240
It would even enable us to head to the front lines against Japan.

221
15:38.240 --> 15:40.920
We previously proposed to the 4th Front Army

222
15:40.950 --> 15:42.700
that it take the lead

223
15:42.720 --> 15:44.720
in swiftly occupying Longde,

224
15:44.790 --> 15:47.190
Jingning, Huining and Tongwei,

225
15:47.270 --> 15:48.600
and securing the Xi'an-Lanzhou Highway,

226
15:48.600 --> 15:51.630
so that our 3 main forces could reunite.

227
15:51.840 --> 15:54.300
But Zhang Guotao has been dragging his feet.

228
15:54.390 --> 15:55.870
His troops in southern Gansu

229
15:55.870 --> 15:57.730
have remained idle all this time.

230
15:57.910 --> 15:58.720
Zhang Guotao

231
15:59.530 --> 16:02.550
is back to his old habit of being afraid to confront Hu Zongnan.

232
16:02.550 --> 16:03.480
We must not let

233
16:03.500 --> 16:06.770
the tragedy of the planned Songpan Campaign happen again.

234
16:07.250 --> 16:08.220
Keep pressing them.

235
16:08.220 --> 16:10.680
If the 4th Front Army won't commit or take action,

236
16:10.680 --> 16:12.140
we'll keep pressing them.

237
16:12.790 --> 16:14.270
Comrade Zedong agrees.

238
16:14.600 --> 16:15.760
We must push them with both telegrams

239
16:15.760 --> 16:16.640
and action.

240
16:16.990 --> 16:19.600
Have Nie Rongzhen lead a special detachment of the 1st Army Corps

241
16:19.600 --> 16:20.550
to occupy Jieshipu

242
16:20.550 --> 16:21.610
and meet them as they march north.

243
16:21.610 --> 16:22.420
Good.

244
16:25.440 --> 16:27.550
Under pressure from the Central Committee,

245
16:27.550 --> 16:30.670
from September 16 to 18, 1936,

246
16:31.240 --> 16:32.910
the Northwest Bureau of the CPC Central Committee

247
16:32.910 --> 16:36.150
held a meeting at Sanshilipu in Min County, Gansu.

248
16:36.150 --> 16:37.010
At the meeting,

249
16:37.050 --> 16:39.780
Zhu De and the overwhelming majority argued their case forcefully,

250
16:39.780 --> 16:41.360
insisting on marching north.

251
16:41.360 --> 16:43.950
Chen Changhao also made it clear

252
16:43.970 --> 16:47.000
that he would follow the Central Committee's order to march north.

253
16:47.000 --> 16:49.660
This caught Zhang Guotao completely off guard.

254
16:49.730 --> 16:51.790
The meeting eventually passed a resolution

255
16:51.790 --> 16:52.440
and issued the

256
16:52.440 --> 16:55.870
Campaign Plan for the Tongwei, Zhuanglang, Jingning and Huining Areas.

257
16:55.870 --> 16:58.080
The 4th Front Army planned to move north in its entirety

258
16:58.080 --> 17:01.150
along the Dingxi-Huining-Jingning line.

259
17:02.090 --> 17:03.850
But Zhang Guotao

260
17:03.870 --> 17:07.310
still hadn't abandoned his plan to march west.

261
17:12.030 --> 17:13.069
Comrade Guotao.

262
17:13.790 --> 17:14.920
You wanted to see me?

263
17:15.550 --> 17:16.440
You're here.

264
17:22.670 --> 17:24.010
We're not at the conference now.

265
17:24.010 --> 17:25.339
Why so tense?

266
17:25.599 --> 17:26.770
Come up here.

267
17:41.400 --> 17:42.350
Changhao,

268
17:44.310 --> 17:46.510
I've thought this over again and again.

269
17:47.010 --> 17:48.680
I believe your

270
17:48.700 --> 17:51.500
Jingning-Huining Campaign Plan is ill-advised.

271
17:52.030 --> 17:55.830
You were wrong to reject my plan to march west.

272
17:57.960 --> 17:59.480
We discussed this issue

273
18:00.000 --> 18:01.730
for 3 whole days at the meeting.

274
18:01.810 --> 18:03.550
Everything was made perfectly clear,

275
18:03.550 --> 18:05.380
and the plan was already put to a vote and passed.

276
18:05.380 --> 18:06.720
That was what we discussed at the meeting.

277
18:06.720 --> 18:08.920
Now it's just between you and me.

278
18:09.240 --> 18:10.830
We've worked together for so many years.

279
18:10.830 --> 18:12.350
You can't listen only to Zhu De

280
18:12.350 --> 18:14.030
and refuse to listen to me.

281
18:14.480 --> 18:15.160
All right.

282
18:15.720 --> 18:16.480
Go ahead.

283
18:19.810 --> 18:21.470
Given the current situation,

284
18:22.360 --> 18:25.760
things are extremely unfavorable for our 4th Front Army.

285
18:26.720 --> 18:28.180
If we follow your plan

286
18:28.200 --> 18:29.280
and march north,

287
18:29.680 --> 18:33.680
we'll be facing Hu Zongnan's elite troops.

288
18:34.390 --> 18:35.670
Just look at our men.

289
18:35.960 --> 18:37.640
After over a year of fighting in the south,

290
18:37.640 --> 18:39.240
we've only just crossed the grasslands.

291
18:39.240 --> 18:42.500
How can these tens of thousands of exhausted troops fight?

292
18:42.510 --> 18:44.120
If we cross the Yellow River to the west,

293
18:44.120 --> 18:47.030
we can avoid the enemy's strong forces entirely

294
18:47.350 --> 18:49.660
and establish a route to the outside world.

295
18:49.660 --> 18:51.380
Once our forces grow stronger

296
18:51.720 --> 18:53.650
and we've gained a solid foothold,

297
18:54.240 --> 18:55.840
we'll finally have a chance.

298
18:55.880 --> 18:57.080
If we march north now,

299
18:57.270 --> 18:58.550
we'll have no chance at all.

300
18:58.550 --> 19:01.150
Can't we stop repeating what happened before?

301
19:01.590 --> 19:03.030
Every time a decision is made at a meeting,

302
19:03.030 --> 19:05.710
you go behind everyone's backs and overturn it again and again.

303
19:05.710 --> 19:06.920
Looking back now,

304
19:07.350 --> 19:11.310
many of our previous decisions were wrong.

305
19:12.350 --> 19:14.680
We mustn't keep making the same mistakes.

306
19:17.920 --> 19:19.000
I know.

307
19:20.160 --> 19:21.920
On many issues in the past,

308
19:23.070 --> 19:25.800
some of my judgments were not entirely accurate.

309
19:26.070 --> 19:27.790
But I corrected them in time.

310
19:28.270 --> 19:29.480
The Central Committee...

311
19:29.480 --> 19:30.400
Our so-called "Central Committee"

312
19:30.400 --> 19:31.830
is no longer the Central Committee.

313
19:31.830 --> 19:32.760
Marching north.

314
19:33.070 --> 19:34.350
They told us to march north.

315
19:34.350 --> 19:36.030
And we did.

316
19:36.440 --> 19:37.240
But, Changhao,

317
19:37.240 --> 19:39.440
I can tell you with complete confidence

318
19:39.920 --> 19:41.830
that every decision I made

319
19:41.920 --> 19:43.070
was based entirely on

320
19:43.070 --> 19:45.440
the interests of the 4th Front Army.

321
19:46.110 --> 19:47.710
The reason I thought that way

322
19:48.160 --> 19:50.590
was because I firmly believed

323
19:50.790 --> 19:52.720
that the backbone of our revolution

324
19:52.720 --> 19:54.310
was our 4th Front Army.

325
19:54.480 --> 19:55.550
Not their 1st Front Army,

326
19:55.550 --> 19:57.240
with fewer than 10,000 men.

327
19:57.590 --> 19:59.030
Everything I did

328
19:59.350 --> 20:01.590
was to preserve and strengthen

329
20:01.590 --> 20:04.070
the main force of our revolution.

330
20:04.310 --> 20:05.440
How could I stand by and watch

331
20:05.440 --> 20:07.170
the 4th Front Army be wiped out?

332
20:07.240 --> 20:08.750
If we march north

333
20:08.920 --> 20:09.920
and our forces are wiped out,

334
20:09.920 --> 20:12.750
how are we supposed to survive in northern Shaanxi?

335
20:12.750 --> 20:13.900
Have you ever thought about that?

336
20:13.900 --> 20:16.510
So you've finally said what's really on your mind.

337
20:16.510 --> 20:17.070
Yes.

338
20:17.240 --> 20:18.960
You say you're considering things from the perspective

339
20:18.960 --> 20:20.070
of the 4th Front Army.

340
20:20.070 --> 20:21.400
But that's not all.

341
20:22.240 --> 20:24.570
You have your own personal concerns, too.

342
20:24.640 --> 20:25.830
After all this talk,

343
20:26.030 --> 20:26.790
isn't what you're really afraid of

344
20:26.790 --> 20:28.510
that once we reach northern Shaanxi,

345
20:28.510 --> 20:31.440
they'll hold you accountable for your past actions?

346
20:31.480 --> 20:32.920
Do you really think

347
20:33.740 --> 20:36.700
my concerns are unfounded, Changhao?

348
20:37.440 --> 20:38.880
Aren't you worried, too?

349
20:40.160 --> 20:41.400
Don't forget,

350
20:41.720 --> 20:43.310
I'm the one who put you

351
20:43.720 --> 20:48.350
in the position of political commissar of the 4th Front Army.

352
20:49.120 --> 20:50.980
If they hold anyone accountable,

353
20:51.330 --> 20:52.600
I'll be the first,

354
20:52.620 --> 20:54.220
and you'll be the second.

355
20:55.760 --> 20:57.060
If they strip me of my post,

356
20:57.060 --> 20:58.390
expel me from the Party,

357
20:58.830 --> 20:59.690
put me on trial,

358
21:00.830 --> 21:01.980
or execute me,

359
21:02.350 --> 21:05.400
do you think you'll fare any better, Changhao?

360
21:10.380 --> 21:11.350
Comrade Guotao,

361
21:14.270 --> 21:16.030
I have my own misgivings, too.

362
21:17.720 --> 21:19.980
You're afraid to go to northern Shaanxi.

363
21:21.480 --> 21:22.310
So am I.

364
21:23.400 --> 21:26.440
I've always supported you

365
21:26.550 --> 21:27.550
and trusted you.

366
21:28.310 --> 21:29.840
It was because I trusted you

367
21:30.070 --> 21:31.720
that I've followed you all this way.

368
21:31.720 --> 21:33.000
But don't forget,

369
21:33.750 --> 21:36.150
we're both members of the Communist Party.

370
21:36.890 --> 21:39.050
We must obey Party discipline.

371
21:39.440 --> 21:41.040
If we reach northern Shaanxi

372
21:41.880 --> 21:44.330
and the Central Committee really does hold us accountable,

373
21:44.330 --> 21:46.440
we must admit our mistakes

374
21:47.750 --> 21:51.080
and accept whatever decision the Central Committee makes.

375
22:10.680 --> 22:11.480
Changhao.

376
22:12.510 --> 22:16.440
We've been together for so many years.

377
22:17.310 --> 22:19.440
I've never treated you as an outsider.

378
22:19.550 --> 22:21.000
I have never

379
22:21.830 --> 22:23.160
begged anyone for anything.

380
22:23.160 --> 22:24.310
You know that.

381
22:33.920 --> 22:35.070
But this time,

382
22:35.720 --> 22:36.790
I'm begging you.

383
22:42.560 --> 22:45.480
Give the 4th Front Army a chance.

384
22:46.690 --> 22:48.130
Give yourself a chance,

385
22:48.770 --> 22:50.360
and give me a chance, too.

386
22:51.900 --> 22:54.410
Let's not march north.

387
22:56.030 --> 22:57.430
Let's head west instead.

388
23:03.550 --> 23:04.350
Can we do that?

389
23:20.030 --> 23:20.960
Comrade Guotao,

390
23:21.440 --> 23:25.030
I still stand by the position I took at the meeting.

391
23:26.920 --> 23:27.980
We must march north

392
23:28.550 --> 23:30.040
and reunite with the Central Committee.

393
23:30.040 --> 23:31.580
The Central Committee has just issued

394
23:31.580 --> 23:32.310
the "Resolution of the CPC Central Committee

395
23:32.310 --> 23:34.440
on the New Situation of the Anti-Japanese National Salvation Movement

396
23:34.440 --> 23:36.170
and the Democratic Republic."

397
23:36.240 --> 23:37.300
It also states that

398
23:37.640 --> 23:38.770
splitting the Party

399
23:38.790 --> 23:40.720
would harm the Chinese revolution

400
23:41.590 --> 23:45.590
and go against the directives of the Comintern.

401
23:55.070 --> 23:56.480
Comrade Chen Changhao,

402
24:00.110 --> 24:03.040
what a noble sense of political conviction you have!

403
24:05.110 --> 24:07.200
So this is what you really think.

404
24:07.750 --> 24:10.200
The Comintern is on their side now,

405
24:11.110 --> 24:14.750
so you have to side with them, too.

406
24:15.790 --> 24:16.720
Is that it?

407
24:18.070 --> 24:20.270
You came back from Moscow.

408
24:23.680 --> 24:24.480
Go on, then.

409
24:25.880 --> 24:28.640
Go reunite with them.

410
25:19.000 --> 25:21.080
I, Zhang Guotao,

411
25:23.510 --> 25:25.350
one of the founders of the Party,

412
25:27.270 --> 25:29.330
have lived through momentous times.

413
25:32.400 --> 25:37.200
How could I have come to this?

414
26:16.400 --> 26:19.160
On September 20, 1936,

415
26:19.510 --> 26:22.350
Zhang Guotao went alone to

416
26:22.350 --> 26:25.060
the 4th Front Army's Forward Command Post in Zhangxian.

417
26:25.060 --> 26:28.170
Deliberately concealing the resolution of the Sanshilipu Meeting in Min County,

418
26:28.170 --> 26:29.740
he used his authority as Northwest Bureau Secretary

419
26:29.740 --> 26:31.790
and Political Commissar-General of the Red Army

420
26:31.790 --> 26:34.400
to order the 4th Front Army's Forward Command Post

421
26:34.400 --> 26:38.000
to draw up a new campaign plan to cross the Yellow River westward.

422
26:38.540 --> 26:41.300
From September 24 to 27,

423
26:41.570 --> 26:44.920
the Central Committee, along with Peng Dehuai, Ren Bishi, He Long

424
26:44.920 --> 26:47.050
and other leaders of the 1st and 2nd Front Armies,

425
26:47.050 --> 26:49.030
sent Zhang Guotao several telegrams

426
26:49.030 --> 26:50.660
urging him to reconsider.

427
26:51.130 --> 26:53.130
Furthermore, reconnaissance revealed

428
26:53.130 --> 26:56.790
that crossing the Yellow River to the west was no longer feasible.

429
26:56.880 --> 26:58.480
On the night of September 27,

430
26:58.850 --> 27:01.440
Zhu De, Zhang Guotao, Xu Xiangqian

431
27:01.470 --> 27:04.510
and Chen Changhao jointly sent a telegram to the Central Committee,

432
27:04.510 --> 27:06.940
titled "On Carrying Out the Central Committee's Order

433
27:06.940 --> 27:08.240
to March North and Reunite."

434
27:08.240 --> 27:09.350
He abandoned the plan to cross westward

435
27:09.350 --> 27:10.810
and turned north instead.

436
27:11.150 --> 27:14.630
Thus, the dispute over marching north or westward,

437
27:14.650 --> 27:18.580
once again stirred up by Zhang Guotao, finally came to an end.

438
27:22.040 --> 27:25.650
[Zhidan County (formerly Bao'an County), Shaanxi]

439
27:28.160 --> 27:30.920
At last, this turmoil is over.

440
27:32.150 --> 27:33.270
Last September,

441
27:34.160 --> 27:36.350
Zhang Guotao used

442
27:36.350 --> 27:38.680
his inability to cross the tiny Gaqu River as an excuse

443
27:38.680 --> 27:40.080
and led his troops south,

444
27:40.110 --> 27:42.350
causing a split between the 1st and 4th Front Armies.

445
27:42.350 --> 27:43.510
One year later, around this time,

446
27:43.510 --> 27:44.570
also in September,

447
27:44.880 --> 27:46.740
unable to cross the Yellow River,

448
27:46.750 --> 27:50.880
Zhang Guotao has returned to the path of reuniting with the 1st Front Army.

449
27:51.000 --> 27:52.350
What a twist of fate!

450
27:53.430 --> 27:56.240
Although this turmoil didn't last long,

451
27:56.400 --> 27:59.270
it gave Hu Zongnan time to advance westward.

452
28:00.110 --> 28:01.160
His main forces

453
28:01.180 --> 28:03.550
have already approached Tongwei and Huining.

454
28:03.550 --> 28:06.200
The 2nd Front Army is now caught between two enemies,

455
28:06.200 --> 28:08.400
and faces the serious risk of being trapped by Hu Zongnan

456
28:08.400 --> 28:11.270
between the Xi'an-Lanzhou Highway and south of the Wei River.

457
28:11.270 --> 28:14.250
We must immediately urge the 2nd Front Army to march north as soon as possible.

458
28:14.250 --> 28:17.160
At the same time, order the main forces of the 1st Front Army

459
28:17.160 --> 28:18.510
to move south and assemble

460
28:18.510 --> 28:20.110
to support the 2nd Front Army.

461
28:20.110 --> 28:23.310
The reunion of all 3 main forces is just around the corner.

462
28:33.980 --> 28:36.270
On October 2, 1936,

463
28:36.640 --> 28:38.720
the cavalry regiment of the 15th Red Army Corps

464
28:38.720 --> 28:41.000
rode for more than 20 hours without stopping

465
28:41.000 --> 28:42.800
and seized Huining County seat.

466
28:43.350 --> 28:44.920
From October 7 to 9,

467
28:45.400 --> 28:48.790
units of the 4th Front Army arrived in Huining one after another

468
28:48.790 --> 28:51.650
and successfully reunited with the 1st Front Army.

469
28:52.590 --> 28:55.050
The Central Committee ordered Chen Geng, commander of the 1st Division

470
28:55.050 --> 28:57.590
to lead the 1st Regiment in garrisoning Huining

471
28:57.590 --> 28:59.160
and welcoming the arrival of Red Army Headquarters

472
28:59.160 --> 29:01.750
and the 4th Front Army Command.

473
29:02.790 --> 29:05.160
On October 9, 1936,

474
29:05.350 --> 29:07.880
Zhu De, Zhang Guotao, Xu Xiangqian

475
29:08.070 --> 29:10.640
and Chen Changhao led Red Army Headquarters

476
29:10.640 --> 29:12.830
and the 4th Front Army General Command

477
29:12.890 --> 29:14.050
into Huining,

478
29:14.820 --> 29:17.540
where they received a warm welcome from the officers and soldiers of the 1st Division.

479
29:17.340 --> 29:20.490
[October 9, 1936; Huining, Gansu]

480
29:25.350 --> 29:27.630
[Chen Geng, Commander of the 1st Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

481
29:37.390 --> 29:38.740
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the 4th Front Army]

482
29:37.880 --> 29:38.680
Chen Geng!

483
29:40.310 --> 29:41.240
Xiangqian!

484
29:49.480 --> 29:50.440
Xiangqian!

485
29:50.620 --> 29:51.930
How did you get so thin?

486
29:53.070 --> 29:53.640
Chen Geng!

487
29:53.640 --> 29:54.840
I'm glad you're back.

488
30:02.020 --> 30:03.080
What a long journey

489
30:04.270 --> 30:05.440
we've had.

490
30:05.640 --> 30:06.440
We're back.

491
30:06.720 --> 30:08.070
That's all that matters.

492
30:08.070 --> 30:09.890
Peng told me something.

493
30:09.920 --> 30:12.510
He said when you met him at the Weigu River,

494
30:12.560 --> 30:14.510
you crossed by sliding along a rope.

495
30:14.510 --> 30:14.980
That's right.

496
30:14.980 --> 30:16.710
If I'd known you had that skill,

497
30:17.030 --> 30:18.550
I'd have strung a 400-kilometer rope crossing for you.

498
30:18.550 --> 30:19.750
You could've slid all the way here,

499
30:19.750 --> 30:21.000
fast and safe.

500
30:22.630 --> 30:23.720
I'm just glad you're back.

501
30:23.720 --> 30:24.720
Fourteen months.

502
30:25.480 --> 30:27.080
Fourteen months is too long.

503
30:27.580 --> 30:28.580
Far too long.

504
30:29.440 --> 30:30.240
Changhao.

505
30:31.880 --> 30:32.940
Comrade Chen Geng.

506
30:33.590 --> 30:35.160
Thank you for coming to welcome us.

507
30:35.160 --> 30:37.330
We're family. No need to stand on ceremony.

508
30:37.330 --> 30:38.130
Chen Geng!

509
30:38.590 --> 30:39.270
Chen Geng!

510
30:41.000 --> 30:41.790
Chen Geng!

511
30:42.920 --> 30:44.380
Commander-in-Chief Zhu!

512
30:44.790 --> 30:46.000
Commander-in-Chief Zhu!

513
30:46.000 --> 30:46.790
Chen Geng!

514
30:48.390 --> 30:50.590
Commander-in-Chief Zhu, you're finally back!

515
30:50.490 --> 30:52.240
[Kang Keqing, Zhu De's wife]

516
30:50.790 --> 30:51.590
I'm back.

517
30:52.310 --> 30:52.960
Chen Geng.

518
30:55.060 --> 30:56.990
Chen Geng, let me have a look at you.

519
30:59.240 --> 31:00.960
How are Mao, Enlai and Luofu?

520
31:01.030 --> 31:02.030
They're all well.

521
31:02.040 --> 31:03.400
They've been waiting day and night,

522
31:03.400 --> 31:04.730
hoping you'd come back.

523
31:04.750 --> 31:06.150
At long last, we're back.

524
31:13.580 --> 31:15.040
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

525
31:15.040 --> 31:17.370
How dare that man show his face here again?

526
31:19.870 --> 31:21.770
The Central Committee sent you to welcome us.

527
31:21.770 --> 31:23.630
Don't go shooting your mouth off.

528
31:25.200 --> 31:26.400
I know what I'm doing.

529
31:30.230 --> 31:31.160
Comrade Guotao,

530
31:31.790 --> 31:35.110
the Central Committee has sent Comrade Chen Geng to welcome us.

531
31:35.110 --> 31:36.170
Comrade Chen Geng,

532
31:36.350 --> 31:37.530
thank you for coming all this way.

533
31:37.530 --> 31:38.360
Not at all.

534
31:39.160 --> 31:40.620
You've had it much harder.

535
31:40.680 --> 31:42.170
You marched from north to south,

536
31:42.170 --> 31:43.880
then all the way back north again.

537
31:43.880 --> 31:46.080
You've traveled twice as far as we have.

538
31:48.770 --> 31:49.850
Comrade Chen Geng,

539
31:50.170 --> 31:52.370
I see you still hold a grudge against me.

540
31:52.790 --> 31:53.750
Absolutely not.

541
31:54.440 --> 31:55.920
I hold no grudge against you.

542
31:55.920 --> 31:57.240
If I did,

543
31:57.360 --> 32:00.690
the Central Committee wouldn't have sent me to welcome you.

544
32:10.430 --> 32:11.320
Let me help you down.

545
32:11.320 --> 32:12.160
No, no, no.

546
32:12.160 --> 32:12.960
I can manage.

547
32:38.110 --> 32:39.150
Comrades!

548
32:39.730 --> 32:42.680
The Central Committee's leaders have sent me here to welcome you.

549
32:42.680 --> 32:45.410
Welcome back to the ranks after your march north!

550
32:45.590 --> 32:48.030
Great!

551
32:48.310 --> 32:51.200
Great!

552
32:51.310 --> 32:53.000
Great!

553
32:53.190 --> 32:54.300
Long live the Red Army!

554
32:54.300 --> 32:55.780
Long live unity!

555
32:56.110 --> 32:57.720
Long live the Red Army!

556
32:57.720 --> 32:59.310
Long live unity!

557
32:59.310 --> 33:00.680
Long live unity!

558
33:00.750 --> 33:02.350
Long live the Red Army!

559
33:02.440 --> 33:03.960
Long live unity!

560
33:03.960 --> 33:05.590
Long live the Red Army!

561
33:05.590 --> 33:07.350
Long live unity!

562
33:07.350 --> 33:09.960
Long live the Red Army!

563
33:10.270 --> 33:12.030
Long live unity!

564
33:12.110 --> 33:13.790
Long live unity!

565
33:13.790 --> 33:15.350
Long live the Red Army!

566
33:15.350 --> 33:17.110
Long live unity!

567
33:17.270 --> 33:18.830
Long live the Red Army!

568
34:10.580 --> 34:14.060
The reunion of the 1st and 4th Front Armies in Huining

569
34:14.370 --> 34:15.960
marked the successful conclusion

570
34:15.960 --> 34:17.960
of the 4th Front Army's Long March.

571
34:17.989 --> 34:20.280
Over the course of 1 year and 7 months,

572
34:20.300 --> 34:23.120
the 4th Front Army traveled nearly 5,000 kilometers,

573
34:23.120 --> 34:26.650
fighting across Sichuan, Xikang, Qinghai and Gansu.

574
34:26.820 --> 34:28.130
Due to the influence of Zhang Guotao's

575
34:28.130 --> 34:29.989
erroneous separatist policies,

576
34:30.280 --> 34:31.480
they crossed snow-capped mountains twice

577
34:31.480 --> 34:32.800
and traversed the grasslands 3 times,

578
34:32.800 --> 34:34.800
enduring unimaginable hardships.

579
34:35.679 --> 34:38.480
Shortly after the reunion of the 1st and 4th Front Armies,

580
34:38.480 --> 34:41.070
the 2nd Front Army, which had marched north across the Wei River,

581
34:39.290 --> 34:43.260
[North Bank of the Wei River, Shaanxi]

582
34:41.560 --> 34:43.969
was caught exposed on its flank

583
34:44.000 --> 34:45.780
due to Zhang Guotao's earlier delays.

584
34:45.780 --> 34:47.300
From October 9 to 10,

585
34:47.409 --> 34:49.820
under fierce attacks by KMT troops,

586
34:49.850 --> 34:53.110
it faced the most perilous ordeal of the entire Long March.

587
34:53.489 --> 34:56.699
After suffering tremendous casualties,

588
34:57.120 --> 34:59.690
it finally reached Jiangtaibu

589
34:59.800 --> 35:01.280
on October 22, 1936,

590
35:01.300 --> 35:04.450
where it reunited with the 1st Front Red Army.

591
35:05.320 --> 35:06.130
At this point,

592
35:06.770 --> 35:08.440
the 3 main forces of the Red Army

593
35:08.440 --> 35:10.900
had finally completed their grand reunion.

594
35:12.380 --> 35:15.380
In 1996, with the approval of the Central Committee,

595
35:15.850 --> 35:17.610
October 22nd

596
35:17.640 --> 35:22.240
was designated as the anniversary of the successful conclusion of the Long March.

597
35:25.450 --> 35:28.750
[Xi'an, Shaanxi]

598
35:48.860 --> 35:49.930
Salute!

599
35:58.330 --> 35:59.210
At ease!

600
36:00.920 --> 36:02.850
I hear you've been very busy lately.

601
36:02.850 --> 36:04.910
Busy during the day and even at night.

602
36:05.000 --> 36:07.400
You've managed to let the 3 main Communist forces reunite

603
36:07.400 --> 36:09.440
right under my nose.

604
36:10.230 --> 36:12.090
Quite an achievement, I must say.

605
36:15.400 --> 36:17.600
I've indeed been working day and night,

606
36:17.630 --> 36:19.070
always keeping in mind your promise

607
36:19.070 --> 36:20.880
to me in Chongqing, Generalissimo:

608
36:20.880 --> 36:22.510
to join forces in resisting Japan

609
36:22.510 --> 36:23.630
and turn the tide.

610
36:24.560 --> 36:25.920
Turn the tide?

611
36:26.820 --> 36:27.570
Excellent!

612
36:27.940 --> 36:29.730
Those words deserve to be engraved

613
36:29.730 --> 36:32.250
on a silver shield-shaped trophy.

614
36:32.300 --> 36:33.360
Shall I present it to you,

615
36:33.360 --> 36:34.960
or should they?

616
36:40.230 --> 36:41.840
The grass sways with the wind.

617
36:41.840 --> 36:43.630
Soldiers follow their commanders.

618
36:43.630 --> 36:46.280
The key to defeat the Communists isn't the soldiers,

619
36:46.280 --> 36:47.590
but the commanders!

620
36:48.390 --> 36:49.650
It's about obedience!

621
37:03.220 --> 37:05.010
As soldiers of the Party,

622
37:05.760 --> 37:07.420
the first thing you must learn

623
37:07.800 --> 37:11.060
is to understand honor and duty, and know right from wrong.

624
37:12.150 --> 37:14.280
At home, you must be filial to your parents.

625
37:14.280 --> 37:16.280
Outside, you must obey your superiors.

626
37:16.280 --> 37:17.680
That's a soldier's duty.

627
37:18.230 --> 37:20.760
There's one more thing I'd like to emphasize.

628
37:20.960 --> 37:22.070
As soldiers,

629
37:22.510 --> 37:25.150
we must know which enemies pose the most immediate threat

630
37:25.150 --> 37:27.080
and which threats are most urgent.

631
37:27.150 --> 37:28.670
At present,

632
37:29.190 --> 37:31.650
the Communists are our most immediate enemy

633
37:31.800 --> 37:33.190
and most urgent threat.

634
37:33.590 --> 37:36.760
The Japanese, by contrast, are a more distant threat.

635
37:36.430 --> 37:38.180
[Yang Hucheng, Director of the Kuomintang's Xi'an Pacification Headquarters]

636
37:37.110 --> 37:38.840
Their threat is not yet urgent.

637
37:39.230 --> 37:42.400
That's why we must pacify the interior before resisting foreign aggression.

638
37:42.400 --> 37:44.280
Anyone who refuses to actively fight the Communists

639
37:44.280 --> 37:46.110
and merely pays lip service to resisting Japan

640
37:46.110 --> 37:48.760
is disobeying orders.

641
37:49.070 --> 37:51.550
That is an act of disloyalty and a failure of filial duty.

642
37:51.550 --> 37:53.280
If we have soldiers like that,

643
37:53.550 --> 37:56.670
the Party will surely punish them.

644
37:57.400 --> 37:58.670
You should all be aware

645
37:59.000 --> 38:02.590
that the Communist Army has now entered Shaanxi and Gansu.

646
38:03.880 --> 38:06.070
Although this is unexpected,

647
38:06.760 --> 38:09.150
it isn't necessarily a bad thing.

648
38:09.400 --> 38:12.190
We must now focus all our efforts,

649
38:12.400 --> 38:13.880
raise our morale,

650
38:14.320 --> 38:15.630
and throw everything we've got into

651
38:15.630 --> 38:18.360
wiping out the Communist Army right here.

652
38:19.960 --> 38:21.590
That is why I've come.

653
38:22.230 --> 38:24.090
Does anyone have any objections?

654
38:34.710 --> 38:35.440
Gentlemen,

655
38:35.880 --> 38:37.550
please follow me to the operations room.

656
38:37.550 --> 38:39.100
I'll explain in detail

657
38:39.150 --> 38:40.400
the Tongwei Campaign Plan personally drawn up

658
38:40.400 --> 38:41.690
by the Generalissimo.

659
38:46.880 --> 38:47.920
Hanqing.

660
38:49.360 --> 38:50.670
Stay for a moment.

661
39:03.240 --> 39:04.880
Someone told me

662
39:05.110 --> 39:06.440
that lately

663
39:06.440 --> 39:09.440
you've been in frequent contact with the Communists.

664
39:09.730 --> 39:11.730
They advised me to keep an eye on you,

665
39:12.300 --> 39:15.030
for fear you might do something to harm the Party.

666
39:15.480 --> 39:17.440
I'm not sure what exactly

667
39:17.460 --> 39:19.520
would constitute harming the Party.

668
39:23.190 --> 39:24.590
I know you well.

669
39:26.710 --> 39:28.510
You're not like Li and Bai.

670
39:29.130 --> 39:30.920
You don't have any hidden agendas.

671
39:30.920 --> 39:32.800
And you would never disregard

672
39:32.800 --> 39:34.760
the brotherhood between us.

673
39:34.960 --> 39:35.650
Would you?

674
39:36.310 --> 39:36.830
Come.

675
39:37.440 --> 39:38.100
Have a seat.

676
39:52.800 --> 39:54.840
But have you ever thought about this?

677
39:54.840 --> 39:56.480
Even Li and Bai, for all their differences,

678
39:56.480 --> 40:00.480
still have to follow the Nationalist Government's orders, don't they?

679
40:02.760 --> 40:04.510
I remember Li Zongren saying

680
40:04.530 --> 40:06.260
in his peace proclamation that

681
40:06.280 --> 40:07.400
the threat of civil war

682
40:07.400 --> 40:08.590
is like an arrow on a taut bowstring.

683
40:08.590 --> 40:09.850
The people are anxious and bewildered,

684
40:09.850 --> 40:11.610
and both China and the world are deeply concerned.

685
40:11.610 --> 40:12.560
Hanqing,

686
40:13.550 --> 40:15.080
we're both reasonable men.

687
40:15.270 --> 40:16.540
I kept you here

688
40:16.650 --> 40:20.740
so you could tell me what you really think.

689
40:22.150 --> 40:23.280
Our nation is facing a grave crisis.

690
40:23.280 --> 40:24.480
We're at a critical juncture.

691
40:24.480 --> 40:25.400
Only by ending the civil war

692
40:25.400 --> 40:25.880
and uniting against foreign aggression

693
40:25.880 --> 40:27.090
can China have any hope.

694
40:27.090 --> 40:28.690
This isn't just my position.

695
40:29.050 --> 40:31.970
It's also the position of our Northeastern Army comrades.

696
40:31.970 --> 40:35.120
These days, the mere mention of resisting Japan gets everyone fired up.

697
40:35.120 --> 40:38.280
But mention fighting the Communists, and morale plummets.

698
40:38.280 --> 40:40.340
What did I say at the airport just now?

699
40:40.530 --> 40:42.660
"Soldiers follow their commanders!"

700
40:42.690 --> 40:45.550
That's because you yourself aren't committed to fighting the Communists!

701
40:45.550 --> 40:47.410
How am I supposed to be committed?

702
40:47.590 --> 40:49.790
You say refusing to fight the Communists is disloyal and unfilial.

703
40:49.790 --> 40:52.360
How many of our men have died fighting the Communists,

704
40:52.360 --> 40:53.190
while their own hometowns

705
40:53.190 --> 40:55.000
remain under Japanese occupation?

706
40:55.000 --> 40:57.430
In the eyes of their parents, wives, and children,

707
40:57.430 --> 40:59.260
in the eyes of their fellow townspeople,

708
40:59.260 --> 41:00.520
can they truly be called loyal and filial?

709
41:00.520 --> 41:02.160
How dare you!

710
41:12.660 --> 41:14.120
I'll give you two choices.

711
41:14.300 --> 41:15.050
First,

712
41:15.180 --> 41:17.170
you and Yang Hucheng take your troops

713
41:17.170 --> 41:18.700
to the Shaanxi-Gansu front

714
41:18.710 --> 41:20.030
and launch an all-out campaign against the Communists.

715
41:20.030 --> 41:20.670
Second,

716
41:20.720 --> 41:22.990
you move your troops to Fujian,

717
41:23.010 --> 41:24.740
and Yang Hucheng goes to Anhui.

718
41:24.860 --> 41:26.170
The entire Northwest region

719
41:26.170 --> 41:28.170
will be taken over by the Central Army.

720
41:28.170 --> 41:29.250
Hanqing.

721
41:29.870 --> 41:31.270
You know what's at stake.

722
41:32.200 --> 41:34.200
Think carefully before you decide.

723
41:42.680 --> 41:44.070
Plain boiled water.

724
41:44.650 --> 41:46.090
Bland and tasteless.
